    "result_text": "The build passes. The full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the audit-on-create requirement in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`:\n\n1. **Added an `AUDIT` logger** \u2014 a static SLF4J logger named `\"AUDIT\"` (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java:76-82`), matching the logger name the test's `AuditLogCapture` attaches to.\n\n2. **Emitted the audit line on successful create** \u2014 right after `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` (so the id has been assigned), the controller logs a single line carrying the owner id, `customerCode`, and `registrationDate`:\n\n   ```java\n   AUDIT.info(\"Owner created: id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={}\",\n       owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate());\n   ```\n\nPlacing it after the persistence and all the reject-guards ensures the line is emitted only on a genuinely successful create. The `AcceptanceTest.coreLogsAuditOnCreate` test passes \u2014 the captured line (e.g. `Owner created: id=11 customerCode=TOW-SUR-0001 registrationDate=2026-08-14`) contains the id, customerCode, and registrationDate exactly as read back from `GET /api/owners/{id}`, and the overall build reports `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
